# sets2 — SINTER, SUNION and the *STORE variants
#
# Learn: SINTER returns members present in ALL given sets, SUNION members
# in ANY of them, SDIFF those in the first but none of the others. Each
# has a *STORE form (SINTERSTORE dest k1 k2) that saves the result as a
# new set instead of returning it.
#
# Task: following:alice and following:bob hold who each of them follows.
#  1. Print the accounts BOTH alice and bob follow.
#  2. Save everyone that alice OR bob follows into reach:alice:bob.
# The two lines below have it the wrong way round.
#

SUNION following:alice following:bob
SINTERSTORE reach:alice:bob following:alice following:bob
